GitHub's answers to `GET /repos/<owner>/<name>`, as `curl --include` prints them (the status line,
the headers and the body, with CRLF line ends). The credential helper's fork read
(gitcredential_fork.go) reads them, and the tests of gitcredential_test.go serve them from a
stand-in curl; gh_notfound_test.go serves not-found.http as the leak guard's curl read's 404.

This repository is public, so no file here carries an outside person's login or the company's
name, and this file names the captured repositories by what they are rather than by their names.
Each capture was copied in with only these values replaced: each replaced account's login, its
numeric id, its node_id and its avatar id, and the host of the repository's homepage.

  - the person whose fork is captured           -> outside-author (id 1000001)
  - the owner of the fork of a fork             -> outside-author (id 1000001)
  - the organization that fork was made from    -> outside-org (id 1000002)
  - the organization of the repository no fork  -> Outside-Org (id 1000002), its case kept
  - the organization the forks are made from    -> acme (id 1000003)
  - the homepage's host                         -> acme.example

The captures were made on 2026-11-19 between 22:13:13Z and 22:13:36Z, in an INFRA issue pod, with
this command and the implement App's installation token on curl's standard input:

  agent-secrets LEGION_IMPLEMENT_APP --github-owner cybermonklabs --github-repo legion \
    --github-read-only --github-token --ttl 15m --reason '<why>' -- sh -c \
    'printf "Authorization: Bearer %s\n" "$LEGION_IMPLEMENT_APP" | /usr/bin/curl -q --no-netrc -sS \
     --include --proto =https -H @- -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
     -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" https://api.github.com/repos/<repository>'

  fork-of-a-served-repository.http  a person's fork, whose parent and source are both the
                                    repository it was made from (acme/oss-verify).
  fork-of-a-fork.http               a fork of an organization's fork, whose parent
                                    (outside-org/oss-verify) and source (acme/oss-verify) differ.
  not-a-fork.http                   an organization's repository that is no fork, asked for in
                                    lower case: its full_name differs from the name asked in case
                                    alone (Outside-Org/libdiginet).
  not-found.http                    a repository of the same person that does not exist: 404.
  moved.http                        repos/sjawhar/legion, which GitHub moved to another owner: 301,
                                    which curl does not follow.
  bad-credentials.http              the person's fork, read with a bearer token GitHub does not
                                    know, an invented word in place of the secret: 401.

Two answers GitHub cannot be made to give on demand are derived from not-found.http. Each has the
status line `HTTP/2 403`, the headers and the body named here, and content-length set to the new
body's length:

  core-limit-spent.http             x-ratelimit-remaining: 0 and x-ratelimit-reset: 1794636000, and
                                    the body of curlRateLimited
                                    (internal/leakguard/visibility_transport_test.go).
  secondary-limit.http              retry-after: 60, and a body whose message is the secondary
                                    limit's words in internal/leakguard/visibility_graphql_test.go.
